From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:27:32 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: CBM probe and datapath bring-up orchestration

Add cbm.c, the platform driver for the buffer manager node, and the
bring-up sequence tying together everything added so far. The marked
constraints in the order below are load-bearing: each one was
established by breaking TX or RX on this hardware.

Probe sequence:

 1. Map the eleven register windows, each by name, and take the gate
    clock by name.
 2. Map the reserved-memory buffer pools.
 3. TOE/DMA3 controller reset parity (matching the vendor hdma
    probe environment) BEFORE the CBM hardware init.
 4. cbm_hw_init() writes the NGI endian mask and the interface mux
    first, because both are sampled at block reset, then runs FSQM init
    for both segment sizes, init_cbm_basic (pool base registers incl.
    the IOCU aliases, JSEL, counter zero-fill, interrupt mapping and the
    CBM interrupt, live from this point), EQM CPU ports 0-3 (must
    precede the first FSQM buffer pop), EQM DMA ingress ports 5-8
    standard+jumbo with descriptor seeds, and the TOE (IGP9) and LDMA
    (IGP15) ports.
 5. tmu_init().
 6. QIDT baseline: fill the whole queue-selection cube with the
    drop value, then run the CPU DQM row walk (queues 35/34/36)
    and the endpoint-7 route to queue 35 - routes are carved out
    of an all-drop baseline, never the reverse.
 7. Bring up one CPU dequeue port per online CPU, so each CPU
    returns segments through its own ptr_rtn register.
 8. Preconfigure the dequeue port and flat TMU egress path of every
    datapath port the switch macros' port children name, skipping
    the CPU port. Egress must be configured BEFORE the controllers
    are enabled.
 9. cbm_enable_controllers() enables the DQM, then the EQM, then the
    enqueue-delay setting that lets the TMU bind body lengths. The
    four load-spreader interrupt enables are written to zero, because
    those lines are level-sourced and no handler is registered for
    them, and the per-port EQM and DQM interrupts are masked.
10. hdma_port_enable() opens each preconfigured port's egress
    channel once, at the end of probe, after the TMU egress port
    exists - the channel is never toggled afterwards (toggling it
    desynchronizes the dequeue handshake).
11. The eight EQM RX-admit movers open, DMA2RX ch14/15 (standard)
    and ch30/31 (jumbo) into IGP5/6, DMA1RX ch0/6 into IGP7 and
    ch5/11 into IGP8.
12. Give the conduit children of the node their devices.

RCU_IAP_WDT_RST_EN, which gates the watchdog's reset request, is left to
the watchdog driver that owns it.

The platform driver is registered under a name of its own rather than
the device's, because two platform drivers cannot share a name.

Nothing builds this driver yet. The next change wires the buffer manager
into the build.

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
cqm/grx500/cbm.c probe/config-walk code, which carries no copyright
notice of its own; the file header names it as the origin and
per-function provenance is recorded in comments. One deviation from
the vendor order is deliberate and safe: the EQM is armed earlier
than the vendor arms it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

